This is an extension of #4687
Spark actions also manipulate the table obj, apart of SparkWrite and hence, the handling of CommitStateUnknown exception when encountered, should not delete the added files.
While actions such as RewriteDatafiles have this handling :

      iceberg/core/src/main/java/org/apache/iceberg/actions/RewriteDataFilesCommitManager.java

        Lines 108 to 120
      in
      566b2fe

           public void commitOrClean(Set<RewriteFileGroup> rewriteGroups) {

             try {

               commitFileGroups(rewriteGroups);

             } catch (CommitStateUnknownException e) {

               LOG.error("Commit state unknown for {}, cannot clean up files because they may have been committed successfully.",

                   rewriteGroups, e);

               throw e;

             } catch (Exception e) {

               LOG.error("Cannot commit groups {}, attempting to clean up written files", rewriteGroups, e);

               rewriteGroups.forEach(this::abortFileGroup);

               throw e;

             }

           }

